cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "LMU SMART RAG"
message: >-
  If you use this software, or parts of it, please cite it as below. The
  license additionally requires that the Required Notice line in LICENSE
  travels with any copy you pass on.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Götzinger"
    given-names: "Benjamin"
    affiliation: >-
      DigiLLab, Chair of Empirical Education and Educational Psychology
      (Prof. Frank Fischer), LMU München
abstract: >-
  A self-hosted retrieval-augmented generation system for university courses.
  Course material is ingested into a vector store and a concept graph, and
  course-specific agents answer from it; the installation is driven by a
  bootstrap wizard and integrates into an LMS via LTI 1.3.
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - higher education
  - teacher education
  - self-hosted
  - LTI 1.3
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-08-27"
